   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Stance first, arguments afterwards",
     "texto": [
      "When two texts deal with the same issue, the first thing is to know what each one argues for. If you start with the details, you get lost.\n\nThe order that works is this one:\n\n1. **The stance**: one sentence. «Este texto defiende que el móvil siga accesible».\n2. **The arguments**: why it says so. «Porque hay quien lo necesita para participar».\n3. **The concession**: what it admits from the other side. «Aunque reconoce que distrae».\n\nThe concession is the piece that is hardest to see, and the one that gives the most information: a text that concedes something is not a naive text, it is qualifying its position."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Conceding is not changing your mind",
     "texto": [
      "**The concession** is acknowledging a valid point from the other side without abandoning your own stance. It is marked with connectors:\n\n- **aunque** + indicative (a real fact): «Mantiene su postura, aunque reconoce el problema».\n- **aunque** + subjunctive (a hypothesis): «Aunque reconozca el problema, mantiene su postura».\n- **pero**, **sin embargo**, **no obstante**: they come afterwards and announce the turn.\n- **es cierto que… pero**: the classic formula of concession.\n\nNotice the difference: with the indicative, the speaker accepts the fact; with the subjunctive, they present it as something that does not affect them."
     ],
